.TH SUPERHOLD 1 "September 2026" "Superhold 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
superhold \- contextual shortcut guide shown while holding a key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B superhold
.RI "[daemon|dump|preview|status] [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Hold Super alone for half a second to show shortcuts for the focused application
and desktop. Release it or press another key to dismiss the guide. The window
does not take keyboard focus. Use the pointer wheel to scroll long sections.
.PP
The Sway backend uses readable evdev keyboards and compositor IPC. The X11
backend uses XInput2 raw key events, XQueryKeymap and EWMH window properties, with Openbox and LXQt
configuration where available. Application profiles explicitly label partial
coverage. Unsupported Wayland compositors are not silently treated as Sway.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run the hold-to-show service for this graphical session.
.TP
.B dump
Print a JSON snapshot of the current shortcut context.
.TP
.B preview
Show the current context briefly without waiting for the hold key.
.TP
.B status
Report whether a matching service is running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--trigger " "super|capslock"
Observe this physical key without changing keyboard mappings or Caps Lock state.
.TP
.BI "--backend " "auto|sway|x11"
Select the graphical session backend.
.TP
.BI "--config " PATH
Read settings from this TOML file.
.TP
.BI "--profiles " PATH
Read additional application shortcut profiles from this JSON file.
.TP
.BI "--socket " PATH
Use this Sway IPC socket.
.TP
.BI "--seconds " NUMBER
Set the preview duration.
.TP
.BI "--hold-seconds " NUMBER
Override the configured hold duration (0.15 to 3 seconds).
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/superhold/config.toml
contains trigger, hold_seconds and backend settings.
.I ~/.config/superhold/profiles.json
contains user application profiles. XDG_CONFIG_HOME overrides ~/.config.
.SH THEMING
Uses the Qt application palette, fonts and style. Configure these with your
desktop's appearance settings or qt6ct. The program does not select a platform
theme or force a particular palette. Desktop plugins vary in whether changes
are broadcast to running applications; restart the guide if your plugin only
loads settings at startup.
.SH SECURITY
Run as the desktop user, never as root. Sway requires existing read access to
keyboard devices. The package does not grant device permissions or add users
to the input group. Key contents are not logged or sent over the network.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sway (1),
.BR openbox (1),
.BR qt6ct (1)
